-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Third-party material included in the app

The texts, dictionaries and fonts inside the app are not covered by the
licence above. They keep their own licences:

- King James Version: public domain.
- Greek New Testament: 1894 Scrivener Textus Receptus with Strong's tagging.
- Hebrew Old Testament: Open Scriptures Hebrew Bible (Westminster Leningrad
  Codex), CC BY 4.0.
- Hebrew Strong's dictionary and Brown-Driver-Briggs (1906, public domain),
  digital text by the Open Scriptures Hebrew Lexicon, CC BY 4.0.
- Greek Strong's dictionary: Open Scriptures JSON edition, CC BY-SA.
- Vine's Expository Dictionary of New Testament Words (1940): public domain.
- Cross-references: Treasury of Scripture Knowledge, via OpenBible.info,
  CC BY.
- Tagalog: Tagalog Unlocked Literal Bible (banal na Bibliya),
  © 2018 Door43 World Missions Community, CC BY-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0). Shown as published,
  arranged by the KJV's verses (Numbers 14:36-37 joined; Revelation 12:18
  and 3 John 15 shown in Revelation 13:1 and 3 John 14).
- Book and chapter introductions: Matthew Henry, An Exposition of the Old and
  New Testaments (1706-1721; Romans to Revelation completed from his notes by
  other ministers), public domain; text from the Christian Classics Ethereal
  Library.
- Fonts: "Koine Reader" (a subset of Gentium, SIL Global), "English Reader"
  (a subset of Gentium Plus, SIL International), Ezra SIL and IM Fell,
  under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.

The full list of sources is in the app under Help > Texts and sources.
